    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling Saturday, anchored by the premium efficiency of **Gunnar Henderson** (70.72) and **Jackson Merrill** (67.41). **Gunnar Henderson** faces Gausman, but his elite situational scoring\u2014boosted by a favorable batting order position and the high probability of a stolen base attempt due to the pitcher's slow delivery\u2014keeps him in must-start territory. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Brazob\u00e1n. While we are wary of an elite catcher arm limiting his base-stealing upside, the combination of his high-leverage lineup spot and favorable wind conditions makes him our most efficient outfielder today. **Kyle Tucker** (66.87) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.55) round out our core; both are hitting in optimal spots in the order, and despite the pedigree of their opposing pitchers, their foundational projections remain far too robust to consider anything other than an aggressive start.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Nolan Schanuel** (41.09). While he hovered near our marginal-start threshold, the matchup against Sheehan proved too prohibitive, as the pitcher's elite skills significantly penalized **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s base projection, dropping him just below the cutoff for the utility slot. Meanwhile, we remain hyper-vigilant regarding our stolen base exposure. Both **Sam Antonacci** (56.83) and **Miguel Vargas** (48.58) are facing Nola, and while they hold marginal-to-strong scores, their efficiency is slightly capped by an elite catcher frame. We have opted to run **Sam Antonacci** due to his superior xwOBA and favorable park factors, though we are tracking the risk that elite defensive peripherals will suppress his secondary category production. The rest of the bench\u2014including **Dominic Smith** and **Brayan Rocchio**\u2014remains grounded today due to poor platoon splits and sub-40 scores, preserving our game caps for more opportunistic windows later in the week.",
